WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
2018.

2
00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:06.650
A TV fantasy series helped attract 1 in
every 6 visitors who came to Northern

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.470
Ireland from outside it.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.410
That was about 350,000 people,
spending over 50 million pounds.

5
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:20.090
Making that series, Game of Thrones,
generated 251 million pounds for Northern

6
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.630
Ireland's economy.

7
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.190
Do people only visit real attractions?

8
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.570
Or can a country sell a
story, rather than a place?

9
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.610
In this mission, you'll meet
three national niche strategies:

10
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.350
movie location, adventure
and heritage tourism.

11
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.370
Then you'll go from a bungy bridge near
Queenstown to the set routes that guide

12
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.750
visitors around Machu Picchu.

13
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.030
Your mission: decide whether
a country can sell a story,

14
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.600
and what it takes.
